se</li>\n<li style=\"margin-left: 1.0in;\">Add new parts to Parts Master\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-roman;\">\n<li style=\"margin-left: 1.5in;\">Research parts data (PN, MTBF, DESCRITPITON,</li>\n<li style=\"margin-left: 1.5in;\">EOL/EOSL equipment issues</li>\n<li style=\"margin-left: 1.5in;\">Estimate 200 unique parts @ 5 minutes each = 20 hours</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li style=\"margin-left: 1.5in; text-align: left;\">Construct any feasible alternate support approaches assume 3 @ 12 hours each = 36 hours\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-alpha;\">\n<li style=\"margin-left: 1.0in;\">Lesser service levels with sparing supplements</li>\n<li style=\"margin-left: 1.0in;\">Make recommendations</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li style=\"margin-left: 1.0in;\">Compile and Present value report and any recommendations to PM 8 hours</li>\n</ol>";
            string expectedResult = "1235Review vendor RFPs to understand cost basis (service levels) of 14 Vendors (2 hours each) = 28 hoursWork with GSCO to issue RFP for alternate service levels = 8 hoursDoes not include GSCO hoursNOTE: This should be done during the up from RFPValidate new Unique parts from BOM:Compare to GSMO Approved Parts databaseAdd new parts to Parts MasterResearch parts data (PN, MTBF, DESCRITPITON,EOL/EOSL equipment issuesEstimate 200 unique parts @ 5 minutes each = 20 hoursConstruct any feasible alternate support approaches assume 3 @ 12 hours each = 36 hoursLesser service levels with sparing supplementsMake recommendationsCompile and Present value report and any recommendations to PM 8 hours";

            string actualResult = RTEUtilities.TurnHTMLIntoPlainText(input);

            Assert.AreEqual(expectedResult, actualResult);
        }

